`main.cpp` и `CMakeLists.txt` в этом шаге не трогаем — они остаются следующим этапом.

The user asks: `next()` takes an empty `Tag` object by reference, fills it, returns T/F/malformed. Where does it get the actual text? They want to understand the source of the text: `TagReader` stores `std::string_view xml_` (the whole XML passed to the constructor) and `pos_`; `next()` takes a `std::string_view` slice of `xml_` (`xml_.substr(begin, length)`) and assigns it to `out.text`, `out.name`, etc. The text is not copied; it's a view into the original XML buffer. The caller must keep the XML alive while the reader/tag views are used.

Need to be clear:
- `parse_cobertura(std::string_view xml, ...)` receives the whole report.
- `TagReader reader(xml);` stores `xml_ = xml` (a non-owning view) and `pos_ = 0`.
